  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "When Tang clan’s Tang Fang Ming is trapped in Thieving Heaven Demon Venerable’s dream realm, first supreme elder Tang Yang lists three ways to keep him alive. Tang Miao tells the elders to go back first. Alone, she judges that asking White Sea Shatuo has some hope. She thinks he has high dream path proficiency, that her brother praised him many times in private, and that asking him would cost a huge price. She also thinks only the Paradise Earth Immortal Venerable inheritance in the siblings’ hands can move him.",
      "chapters": [
        775
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_tang_clan",
        "char_tang_fang_ming",
        "char_thieving_heaven_demon_venerable",
        "char_tang_yang",
        "char_paradise_earth_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is an old and skinny man, barefooted in the sky, with a white cloth on his head and white bandages on his forearms and legs. His gaze is deep.",
      "chapters": [
        864
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Invaders break a crack in a green sky above a featherman city. Their leader is an old, skinny, barefooted Gu Immortal with a white cloth on his head and white bandages on his forearms and legs. The others answer him as Lord White Sea Shatuo. He orders the attack. After three days and two nights, one featherman Gu Immortal is dead and the other two fall back on Sacred Feather City, a huge Immortal Gu House, to resist his group.",
      "chapters": [
        864
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "sacred-feather-siege",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "house_sacred_feather_city",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Tang Yang Ran asks whether to interrupt the feathermen’s coming move. He says he had predicted the situation, that he wants the Immortal Gu House, and that they should keep attacking without interrupting the escape. The feathermen activate heavenly wish and leave. An empty Sacred Feather City remains, and he obtains the house.",
      "chapters": [
        865
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "immortal-gu-house-acquired",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "move_heavenly_wish"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later knows the green heaven fragment’s scenery well enough to reach it with Fixed Immortal Travel, but treats the place as a lion’s den while White Sea Shatuo and other Gu Immortals occupy it.",
      "chapters": [
        903
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "reputation-as-a-deterrent",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "gu_fixed_immortal_travel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Western Desert immortals besiege Sacred Feather City with battlefield killer moves. His methods immobilize the house so it cannot break free quickly. When a gap opens in the wall, Zhou Zhong goes to it. The featherman first supreme elder enters to save him. White Sea Shatuo then appears beside that elder, and his aura erupts to show rank eight cultivation level.",
      "chapters": [
        977
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "western-desert-battle",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_western_desert",
        "char_zhou_zhong"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Tang Miao gave up clues to Paradise Earth’s true inheritance and got help from White Sea Shatuo, which kept Tang Fang Ming from dying in the dream realm. White Sea Shatuo was a split soul of Spectral Soul Demon Venerable. During the Battle of Yi Tian Mountain he led the Western Desert Shadow Sect members and died on that battlefield.",
      "chapters": [
        1490
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "identity-and-death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
